<title>AUSTRALIA: Comalco to sell unit to Reynolds - paper.</title>
<headline>Comalco to sell unit to Reynolds - paper.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aluminium producer Comalco Ltd planned to sell its Southern Aluminium wheel plant in the Australian state of Tasmania to Reynolds Metals Co of the United States, the Sydney Morning Herald newspaper said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The paper said the sale price would not match the A$50 million originally invested, but a loss on the deal was not expected.</p>
<p>The high-technology plant is located next to Comalco's Bell Bay smelter and has struggled to make a profit since it was commissioned in 1989, with an initial production target of 600,000 wheels a year.</p>
<p>Comalco is 67 percent-owned by Rio Tinto Ltd, formerly known as RTZ Corp Plc/CRA Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
